-name><surname>Leake</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Strebel</surname> <given-names>PM</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Perkins</surname> <given-names>BA</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Wharton</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name> <article-title><italic>Haemophilus influenzae</italic> invasive disease in the United States, 1994&#x02013;1995: near disappearance of a vaccine-preventable childhood disease.</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source> <year>1998</year>;<volume>4</volume>:<fpage>229</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>37</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9621193</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Millar</surname> <given-names>EV</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>O&#x02019;Brien</surname> <given-names>KL</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Watt</surname> <given-names>JP</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lingappa</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Pallipamu</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Rosenstein</surname> <given-names>N</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Epidemiology of invasive <italic>Haemophilus influenzae</italic> type A disease among Navajo and White Mountain Apache children, 1988&#x02013;2003.</article-title><source>Clin Infect Dis</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>40</volume>:<fpage>823</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>30</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/428047</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15736015</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Hammitt</surname> <given-names>LL</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Block</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Hennessy</surname> <given-names>TW</given-names></strin