><surname>Hammitt</surname> <given-names>L</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Hennessy</surname> <given-names>T</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Bulkow</surname> <given-names>L</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>DeByle</surname> <given-names>C</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Parkinson</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>The Alaska <italic>Haemophilus influenzae</italic> type b experience: lessons in controlling a vaccine-preventable disease.</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>118</volume>:<fpage>e421</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1542/peds.2006-0287</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16882783</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Galil</surname> <given-names>K</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Singleton</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Levine</surname> <given-names>OS</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Fitzgerald</surname> <given-names>MA</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Bulkow</surname> <given-names>L</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Getty</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Reemergence of invasive <italic>Haemophilus influenzae</italic> type b disease in a well-vaccinated population in remote Alaska.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source> <year>1999</year>;<volume>179</volume>:<fpage>101</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/314569</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9841828</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Lipsitch</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Bacterial vaccines and serotype replacement: lessons from <italic>Haemophi